   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Acceleration of Access to Prevention, Treatment, Care and Support Services - Gambia (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gambia, HIV, ActionAid International The Gambia (AAITG)This program has the following goals: To achieve zero new HIV infections, zero AIDS-related deaths and zero stigma and discrimination in The Gambia. The objectives of this program are: To double the percentage of people showing acceptable attitudes toward people living with HIV by 2019.  To increase the coverage of antiretroviral therapy from 21% to 90% of all persons living with HIV by 2019.  To reduce mother to child transmission of HIV at 6 weeks from 10% to 3% by 2019.  To reduce new HIV infections by 50% among key population by 2019.  To reduce new HIV infections by 50% in the general population by 2019</narrative>
  </description>
